  let p := fun t => (m t + mbar t) / d
  -- for 0 < ε ≤ t: on [ε, t]: δ' + p·δ ≤ 0; M = exp(∫_ε p): (δ·M)' ≤ 0
  -- δ(t) ≤ δ(ε)·exp(−∫_ε^t p) ≤ 2C·(ε/t)²·exp(2C(t−ε)/d)
  -- limit ε → 0
```
The per-ε argument mirrors logDeriv_le_of_le's integrating-factor proof but on [ε,t] with the SIMPLER relation δ' = dm − dmbar ≤ −(m²−mbar²)/d + kbar − k = −p·δ − (k−kbar) ≤ −p·δ — WAIT: dm + m²/d + k ≤ 0 ⟹ dm ≤ −m²/d − k. dmbar = −mbar²/d − kbar. δ' = dm − dmbar ≤ −m²/d − k + mbar²/d + kbar = −(m+mbar)(m−mbar)/d + (kbar−k) = −p·δ − (k−kbar) ≤ −p·δ ✓ (kbar ≤ k).

